Package: noqtis
Type: Package
Title: Post-Quantum Signatures, Key Encapsulation and Signed File Records
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Vansh", "Singh"), "Ruhela", email = "vsruhela@proton.me",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-1750-3592", GitHub = "rootcoder007")),
    person("The noqtis contributors", role = "cph",
           comment = "bundled C library in src/, see inst/COPYRIGHTS"))
Description: Bindings to 'noqtis', a self-contained C11 library for
    post-quantum cryptography: the 'ML-DSA' (FIPS 204) and 'SLH-DSA'
    (FIPS 205) signature schemes, the 'ML-KEM' (FIPS 203) and 'HQC' key
    encapsulation mechanisms, the 'SHA-2' (FIPS 180-4) and 'SHA-3'
    (FIPS 202) hash families and 'HMAC'. It also seals a folder into a
    capsule, a signed record of the exact files it holds, and checks a
    capsule again, so that an analysis can be traced to the data it used.
    The library is bundled; randomness comes from the operating system's
    secure generator, never from R's random number generator.
